{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.SnakeIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.SnakeIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.snake_identity_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.snake_identity_right","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/snake-identity.lean#L37-L46","doc":"**Snake identity (right)**: the composite\n`V∨ →[λ_⁻¹] 𝟙 ⊗ V∨ →[coev ▷ V∨] (V∨ ⊗ V) ⊗ V∨ →[α] V∨ ⊗ (V ⊗ V∨)\n →[V∨ ◁ ev] V∨ ⊗ 𝟙 →[ρ_] V∨`\nequals `𝟙 V∨`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.snake_identity_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.snake_identity_left","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/snake-identity.lean#L23-L35","doc":"**Snake identity (left)**: the composite\n`V →[ρ⁻¹] V ⊗ 𝟙 →[V ◁ coev] V ⊗ (V∨ ⊗ V) →[α⁻¹] (V ⊗ V∨) ⊗ V\n →[ev ▷ V] 𝟙 ⊗ V →[λ_] V`\nequals `𝟙 V`.\n\nThis is the defining property of a right dual (one half of an\nexact pairing). See `RigidMonoidalCategory.snake_left`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:snake-identity","label":"def:snake-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/snake-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}